# Patient Feedback Analysis Template

## 1. Purpose

This template provides a structured approach to analysing patient feedback and translating findings into actionable healthcare quality improvement priorities.

Patient feedback may come from surveys, complaints, compliments, interviews, focus groups, suggestion boxes, patient representatives, or other feedback channels.

The purpose of analysis is not simply to count comments or calculate satisfaction scores. It is to understand patients' experiences, identify recurring problems, recognise strengths, explore potential causes, and support meaningful improvement.

## 2. Objectives

This template helps healthcare teams to:

- Organise patient feedback systematically.
- Identify recurring themes, concerns, and positive experiences.
- Analyse quantitative and qualitative feedback.
- Identify potential inequalities in patient experience.
- Prioritise improvement opportunities.
- Develop measurable actions based on findings.
- Monitor whether actions improve patients' experiences.
- Communicate findings and responses to patients and staff.

